msgid "Modifier order and identity"
msgstr "Modifier order and identity"

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/guide/model-composition.md
msgid "modelRegistry establishes a registry namespace. Adding modelConnection, modelLifecycle or modelAnalytics to an existing definition preserves its records and shares inherited activations. Applying modelRegistry again establishes a separate namespace. Define the final pipeline once; rebuilding it creates different definitions."
msgstr "modelRegistry establishes a registry namespace. Adding modelConnection, modelLifecycle or modelAnalytics to an existing definition preserves its records and shares inherited activations. Applying modelRegistry again establishes a separate namespace. Define the final pipeline once; rebuilding it creates different definitions."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/guide/model-composition.md
msgid "Connections activate in declaration order and release in reverse order. If a later connection fails, earlier connections roll back. Keep dependencies explicit: reading another model does not acquire its connections, and keys do not propagate to dependencies automatically."
msgstr "Connections activate in declaration order and release in reverse order. If a later connection fails, earlier connections roll back. Keep dependencies explicit: reading another model does not acquire its connections, and keys do not propagate to dependencies automatically."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/guide/model-composition.md
msgid "Write a custom modifier"
msgstr "Write a custom modifier"

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/guide/model-composition.md
msgid "A modifier is an ordinary function from ModelSource to ModelDefinition. ModelSource accepts either a pure factory or an existing definition. modelConnection preserves the record and initial types, gives setup the selected store and creation input, and owns its synchronous disposer. It also shares setup across owners and handles rollback between modifiers."
msgstr "A modifier is an ordinary function from ModelSource to ModelDefinition. ModelSource accepts either a pure factory or an existing definition. modelConnection preserves the record and initial types, gives setup the selected store and creation input, and owns its synchronous disposer. It also shares setup across owners and handles rollback between modifiers."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/guide/model-composition.md
msgid "The tracking adapter supplies the transport; the model never imports a socket singleton. Tests can pass a fake feed. The callback receives updates only while the connection is active. The adapter must unsubscribe and ignore late callbacks after cleanup. Setup must undo any partial work before throwing; a cleanup cannot undo work that failed before it was returned."
msgstr "The tracking adapter supplies the transport; the model never imports a socket singleton. Tests can pass a fake feed. The callback receives updates only while the connection is active. The adapter must unsubscribe and ignore late callbacks after cleanup. Setup must undo any partial work before throwing; a cleanup cannot undo work that failed before it was returned."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/guide/model-composition.md
msgid "Use modelLifecycle inside a custom modifier when the task is loading and saving snapshots. Use modelAnalytics for a lazy analytic child. modelConnection is for subscriptions or external handles with synchronous setup and cleanup. Do not use it for values that ion or a derived atom can calculate."
msgstr "Use modelLifecycle inside a custom modifier when the task is loading and saving snapshots. Use modelAnalytics for a lazy analytic child. modelConnection is for subscriptions or external handles with synchronous setup and cleanup. Do not use it for values that ion or a derived atom can calculate."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
