#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/guide/motivation.md
msgid "[Reflect's motivation](https://reflect.effector.dev/learn/motivation) is the direct inspiration for declaring bindings outside components. Holo applies that idea to Jotai; it does not bring Effector's runtime with it."
msgstr "[Reflect's motivation](https://reflect.effector.dev/learn/motivation) is the direct inspiration for declaring bindings outside components. Holo applies that idea to Jotai; it does not bring Effector's runtime with it."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/guide/motivation.md
msgid "[Jotai's performance guide](https://jotai.org/docs/guides/performance) explains why subscription boundaries and cheap renders matter. [React's events and effects guide](https://react.dev/learn/separating-events-from-effects) is useful when deciding whether logic belongs in a command or reactive synchronization. Holo keeps these decisions explicit rather than adding a universal effect abstraction."
msgstr "[Jotai's performance guide](https://jotai.org/docs/guides/performance) explains why subscription boundaries and cheap renders matter. [React's events and effects guide](https://react.dev/learn/separating-events-from-effects) is useful when deciding whether logic belongs in a command or reactive synchronization. Holo keeps these decisions explicit rather than adding a universal effect abstraction."

