#: docs/reference/useImperativeHolo.md
msgid "useImperativeHolo"
msgstr "useImperativeHolo"

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/reference/useImperativeHolo.md
msgid "Keep router, DOM and editor methods inside View. Connect model events to those methods through `holo.imperative`, without storing React functions in atoms."
msgstr "Keep router, DOM and editor methods inside View. Connect model events to those methods through `holo.imperative`, without storing React functions in atoms."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/reference/useImperativeHolo.md
msgid "`useImperativeHolo(imperative, handlers)` exposes a stable method table. Handlers update after commit, without a dependency array. Abandoned renders do not publish handlers. Method names must remain stable. The `imperative` prop is an ordinary typed React ref, supported on React 18 and 19. Each call uses the latest committed props and context, even when holo's own binding props have not changed."
msgstr "`useImperativeHolo(imperative, handlers)` exposes a stable method table. Handlers update after commit, without a dependency array. Abandoned renders do not publish handlers. Method names must remain stable. The `imperative` prop is an ordinary typed React ref, supported on React 18 and 19. Each call uses the latest committed props and context, even when holo's own binding props have not changed."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/reference/useImperativeHolo.md
msgid "`holo.imperative` maps handle methods to eventAtom or actionAtom sources. It does not observe arbitrary writable atoms. Delivery is per View instance, uses the current store and stops when the handle is unavailable. Events are not replayed after mount or Suspense reveal. Two Views observing one source both receive its events; choose one navigation owner deliberately."
msgstr "`holo.imperative` maps handle methods to eventAtom or actionAtom sources. It does not observe arbitrary writable atoms. Delivery is per View instance, uses the current store and stops when the handle is unavailable. Events are not replayed after mount or Suspense reveal. Two Views observing one source both receive its events; choose one navigation owner deliberately."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/reference/useImperativeHolo.md
msgid "Subscriptions are installed before holo activates selected models. Child layout effects are outside that startup ordering. Do not depend on a View handle during unmount. Synchronous throws and rejected handler promises go to `holo.onError`, or console.error when omitted. Publishers do not await View methods."
msgstr "Subscriptions are installed before holo activates selected models. Child layout effects are outside that startup ordering. Do not depend on a View handle during unmount. Synchronous throws and rejected handler promises go to `holo.onError`, or console.error when omitted. Publishers do not await View methods."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/reference/useImperativeHolo.md
msgid "The demo simulates a successful order boundary. In an application, publish orderCreated after the server accepts the order; the View method can call its router instead of selecting a local confirmation screen."
msgstr "The demo simulates a successful order boundary. In an application, publish orderCreated after the server accepts the order; the View method can call its router instead of selecting a local confirmation screen."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/reference/useImperativeHolo.md
msgid "Use imperative methods for behavior that cannot be expressed as state props. Keep ordinary modal visibility in read bindings. The model publishes facts; the View implements platform behavior. See the [runtime migration guide](/runtime) for named models, committed input and ownership."
msgstr "Use imperative methods for behavior that cannot be expressed as state props. Keep ordinary modal visibility in read bindings. The model publishes facts; the View implements platform behavior. See the [runtime migration guide](/runtime) for named models, committed input and ownership."

